# Infisical  →  project harkbell  →  environment prod  →  folder /tls
#
# The Cloudflare Origin Certificate Caddy uses to secure the Cloudflare→origin
# hop on the Harkbell box. Cloudflare terminates the browser's TLS; this pair
# only has to be trusted by Cloudflare, which is why it can run to 15 years and
# why the names it covers must stay proxied (orange cloud).
#
# It used to live only at /opt/vocalonix/certs on the box — outside the repo and
# outside every backup — so tearing the box down destroyed it and rebuilding
# meant a console visit and a hand-copied private key. The deploy installs it
# from here now, on every run, so the box never has to be touched.
#
# Its own folder, not /be: /be is written wholesale to the box's .env and
# forwarded into containers, and a TLS private key has no business in an
# application container's environment.
#
# Base64, not raw PEM: `infisical export --format=dotenv` is one line per value
# and a PEM is multi-line. Raw, it would need \n escaping that has to survive
# two shells and a sed. Base64 round-trips byte-exact.
#
# The voice box needs nothing here — voice.harkbell.com is a DNS-only record, so
# its Caddy gets an ordinary Let's Encrypt certificate over HTTP-01 and renews
# itself.

# To fill or rotate these, from the repo root:
#
#   ./scripts/secrets.sh tls path/to/origin.pem path/to/origin.key
#
# which checks the two actually belong together before uploading anything. By
# hand it is `base64 -w0 origin.pem` (macOS: `base64 -i origin.pem | tr -d '\n'`).
#
# The deploy refuses to run if either is missing, is still REPLACE_ME, is not
# valid base64, does not match its counterpart, or has expired — a bad pair
# otherwise surfaces as a Caddy startup error that reads like a network fault.

ORIGIN_CERT_B64=REPLACE_ME
ORIGIN_KEY_B64=REPLACE_ME
